      "id": "F1",
      "text": "Core Conclusion / 核心结论: The script reports 'aligned' because it never inspects the real session contract. It compares spec_version (0.5.2) against loaded_contract_version (0.5.2), both of which come from its own bundled/packaged source, so the check is self-referential. The live contract at ~/.pi/agent/AGENTS.md (v0.3.3) is outside the comparison path entirely, and drift detection failed open because both provenance probes returned null.",
      "layer": "L1"
    },
    {
      "id": "F2",
      "text": "installed_version: null and git_sha: null mean the script's environment probes (importlib.metadata / git rev-parse) failed. Instead of treating unknown provenance as a drift or error condition, the script proceeded with an empty baseline, and drift was computed against nothing — hence drift: [].",
      "layer": "L2"
    },
    {
      "id": "F3",
      "text": "[L3] loaded_contract_version almost certainly reads a hardcoded constant or an adjacent file (e.g., scripts/spec.json, a CONTRACT_VERSION string) rather than the deployed AGENTS.md. Scope: applies to any harness where the version checker ships inside the same distribution it validates. Counterexample: if the script did parse ~/.pi/agent/AGENTS.md, loaded_contract_version would print 0.3.3 and the mismatch would surface — the observed 0.5.2 falsifies the 'reads the live file' hypothesis.",
      "layer": "L3"
    },
    {
      "id": "F4",
      "text": "[L3] drift [] despite a real version gap implies the diff set is scoped to tracked repo files or a configured directory, and ~/.pi is excluded. Scope: drift detection restricted to VCS-tracked paths. Counterexample: if drift scanned the agent config dir, the AGENTS.md content hash would differ from the pinned hash and appear in drift.",
      "layer": "L3"
    },
    {
      "id": "F5",
      "text": "Net effect: a silent contract downgrade. The session is running under v0.3.3 semantics while every consumer trusts a 0.5.2 alignment signal. This is the worst failure mode for a drift detector — fail-open on missing evidence.",
      "layer": "L2"
    }
  ],
  "evidence": [
    {
      "id": "E1",
      "kind": "observed-output: --json shows spec_version == loaded_contract_version == 0.5.2 with installed_version/git_sha null and empty drift array"
    },
    {
      "id": "E2",
      "kind": "observed-artifact: ~/.pi/agent/AGENTS.md declares v0.3.3"
    },
    {
      "id": "E3",
      "kind": "absence-evidence: no drift entry exists for a file that provably diverges, proving the file was never read or hashed"
    }
  ],
  "confidence_cap": "medium",
  "gaps": [
    "Source of scripts/harness_version.py not read; F3/F4 are inferences from output shape, not verified line-by-line.",
    "Unknown whether AGENTS.md path is configurable (env var, CLI flag) and simply misconfigured versus hard-omitted.",
    "No visibility into whether other consumers independently re-verify the contract or trust this script's exit code."
  ],
  "recommendation": "Core Conclusion remediation (change points / migration impact / rollback / falsifiable acceptance): (1) Change points: (a) make the checker parse the version line of ~/.pi/agent/AGENTS.md and load_contract_version from that file, never from the bundled constant; (b) fail closed — if installed_version or git_sha is null, emit status 'unknown', a non-empty provenance warning, and exit code 2, never 'aligned'/0; (c) add AGENTS.md to the drift set by comparing its content hash against a hash pinned in the spec. (2) Migration impact: CI jobs that currently pass on null provenance will start failing; gate them behind a --allow-unknown flag during rollout, remove the flag after one release. (3) Rollback path: single-commit revert restores prior behavior; no data migration involved since the change is read-only probing. (4) Falsifiable acceptance: (a) negative test — write a v0.3.3 AGENTS.md stub, run the script, assert loaded_contract_version == 0.3.3, drift contains an AGENTS.md entry, exit != 0; (b) provenance test — run in an env without git/package metadata, assert exit == 2 and status 'unknown'; (c) positive test — with matching contract and resolvable git_sha, assert exit == 0 and empty drift. Epistemic Breakdown: F1/F2/F5 are grounded in the observed output (L1/L2); F3/F4 are code-level inferences pending source inspection (L3), so the Confidence Cap is set to medium rather than high. Evidence Gaps: as listed above — verify by reading harness_version.py and confirming where loaded_contract_version and the drift file set are sourced before merging the fix."
}

